  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix UAF in smc_cdc_rx_handler() by pinning the socket (CVE-2026-64541)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA AES cipher key requests (CVE-2026-68452)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA ECC private key requests (CVE-2026-68451)\n  * kernel: wifi: mac80211: validate extension-frame layout before RX (CVE-2026-68470)\n  * kernel: net: qrtr: fix 32-bit integer overflow in qrtr_endpoint_post() (CVE-2026-72298)\n  * kernel: wifi: brcmfmac: cyw: fix heap overflow on a short auth frame (CVE-2026-72003)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: hold event_mutex while checkpointing CRIU events (CVE-2026-74446)\n  * kernel: net: bridge: stop fast-leave after deleting a port group (CVE-2026-74480)\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)\n  * kernel: ipv6: fix use-after-free in ip6_finish_output2() (CVE-2026-80792)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: fix SMI event cross-process information leak (CVE-2026-97422)\n  * kernel: drm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy (CVE-2026-97427)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds for allocate_sdma_queue restore_sdma_id (CVE-2026-97497)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: validate and share PSP fw_pri_buf copies via psp_copy_fw (CVE-2026-97494)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds on allocate_doorbell (CVE-2026-97495)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: Bound GPIO I2C table entry count from VBIOS (CVE-2026-97493)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: fix buffer overflow during vBIOS update (CVE-2026-97425)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Fix OOB memory exposure in get_wave_state() (CVE-2026-97496)\n  * kernel: ALSA: pcm: Serialize PCM mmap with buffer reallocation to fix page UAF (CVE-2026-98116)\n  * kernel: ALSA: ua101: reject mismatched capture/playback packet sizes (CVE-2026-98741)\n  * kernel: net/smc: protect clcsock lifetime in smc_getname (CVE-2026-99032)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via premature connection tracking expiration on TCP RST packets (CVE-2026-99283)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Backport CVEs from v7.2 [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-291553)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
